# Testing with Playwright

Docs: https://playwright.dev/docs/intro and https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/testing/

## Suites

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `tests/e2e/smoke.spec.ts` | Home page renders, document basics, no console errors or hydration warnings, skip link is the first tab stop and moves focus to `main`, tab order reaches every visible control in DOM order without a trap (a radio group is one stop: its checked radio), the page stays light (same colours on every painted element, `color-scheme: light only`) whether the device prefers light or dark |
| `tests/e2e/a11y.spec.ts` | Every built page: axe-core scan with WCAG 2.2 A/AA tags, zero violations (automated subset only) |
| `tests/e2e/motion.spec.ts` | `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` turns off smooth scrolling and leaves no running animation; motion is allowed otherwise, and anything on the document timeline still moving after five seconds must be the home industry strip's scroll or the light on the hero's benefit ring. A scroll-driven animation (the navbar's collapse) moves only as the visitor scrolls, so it is not counted |
| `tests/e2e/seo.spec.ts` | Every built page: title and description lengths, canonical, `lang`, one viewport meta, one `h1`, image `alt`, valid JSON-LD |
| `tests/e2e/layout.spec.ts` | Every built page at 360, 390, 768, 1024, 1440, and 1920 px: no horizontal overflow, no element past the viewport, no clipped text, `h1` in view; writes screenshots to `reports/screenshots/`. Runs under reduced motion and loads every lazy image before each screenshot, so sections show at rest (a full-page capture never scrolls, so a scroll reveal's imagery would otherwise sit tucked away and lazy photos show empty) |
| `tests/e2e/rendering.spec.ts` | Sitemap, robots, favicons served; unknown routes return 404; every internal link on every page resolves |
